      "form_guide": "",
      "comment": "DOONGALLA DON (2) was in the minors two back (29.60) at Sandown but ran below best last time there, finishing 7th. Form from his last run is proving to be solid. Worth another chance. PAY THE REG (1) is a capable type and proved too strong last time to win by 1.5 lengths at Warragul in a handy 26.20 beating Dr. Fallon. Is yet to taste defeat in two starts from this draw. Form should stack up. THAT'S MY BOY (8) tends to drift back and work into the race, finishing out of the placings two back before charging home into the minors latest when third (26.55) in a Grade 4/5 at Warragul last time. Form at the trip sound including four wins. Form from his last run is proving strong. Must be included in calculations. PAW LONNIE (7) cannot be underestimated.",
